        {
          "text": "To elude, or evade by craft; to foil. [Obs.] When misery could beguile the tyrant's rage. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To cause the time of to pass without notice; to relieve the tedium or weariness of; to while away; to divert. Ballads . . . to beguile his incessant wayfaring. W. Irving. entertain.",
